 "verdict": "MEASURED POSITIVE, UNDERPOWERED: at H=126 every book size is positive (yes: worst cell k=200 at +4.09%/yr, best k=50 at +5.24%/yr) and gross grew from +0.28% at H=21 to +2.96% here against an unchanged ~34 bps toll, which is the predicted mechanism. But on NON-OVERLAPPING blocks the t range is +0.75 to +1.33 -- not distinguishable from zero. The monthly t reads higher only because a 126-session return is shared by 6 adjacent monthly blocks. And even that correction is optimistic: at a block width that truly cannot share an outcome this panel holds only 4 blocks, so the honest statement is THE PANEL IS TOO SHORT TO TEST H=126, not 'the t is low'. This is a reason to run it forward in paper at small size, NOT a reason to claim an edge, and NOT a RESEARCH_CLAIM. Incumbent H=21 k=20 was -2.57%/yr.",
 "read_me_first": "Compare the PER-YEAR column, never the per-hold one: a 1% edge per 126 sessions is not better than 0.5% per 21, and the per-hold number alone makes it look it."
}